# Chat frontend environment for `make ui`.
# Copy this file to .env in the same directory. Without a .env file, `make ui`
# offers every agent in .rapid/outputs.json (written by `make deploy`).

# =============================================================================
# OPTION 1: Talk to an agent running on your machine
# =============================================================================
# Start the agent first, from the repository root, e.g.:
#   make docker-run AGENT=customer-support
# LOCAL_AGENT_URL=http://localhost:8080

# =============================================================================
# OPTION 2: Talk to specific deployed runtimes (uses your AWS credentials)
# =============================================================================
# One agent:
# AGENTCORE_RUNTIME_ARN=arn:aws:bedrock-agentcore:us-west-2:XXXXXXXXXXXX:runtime/rapid_v1_customer_support-XXXXXXXXXX
# Several agents (name → runtime ARN):
# AGENT_REGISTRY={"customer-support":"arn:aws:bedrock-agentcore:...","it-helpdesk":"arn:aws:bedrock-agentcore:..."}

# AWS_REGION=us-west-2
